{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":18047,"num_turns":6,"result":"Fixed `lru.py` to implement true LRU semantics; the existing test still passes.\n\nRewrote the cache around a `collections.OrderedDict` instead of a dict plus manual order list:\n\n- `get(key, default=None)` moves the key to the most-recently-used end and returns `default` when the key is missing.\n- `put` on an existing key updates the value and marks it most recently used without evicting; the old code evicted before inserting, which also corrupted its order list with duplicate keys.\n- Eviction now happens only when the size actually exceeds capacity, removing the least-recently-used entry.\n- `__len__` and `__contains__` are implemented, and `in` uses a plain membership check so it does not change recency.\n- `__init__` raises `ValueError` for capacity < 1.\n\nValidation: `python -m pytest -q` passes (1 test), and I exercised each point from the issue with a scratch script (read-refresh preventing eviction, update-without-eviction, missing-key default, `len`/`in`, and the `ValueError`), all passing.","session_id":"fbdbba4c-55d2-4dde-b5fc-20f042426f20","usage":{"input_tokens":2191,"output_tokens":824,"cache_read_input_tokens":56320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"factory_credits":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"ttft_ms":1684.6666666666667}}
